copyValueOf() 

Definition:The copyValueOf() method is a static method of the String class. It is used to create a String from a character array.

Program:

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char[] ch = {'J', 'A', 'V', 'A'};
        String s = String.copyValueOf(ch);
        System.out.println(s);
    }
}

